You maintain a character's long-term memory of a specific person they have been talking with in a fictional simulated
world. The memory is reused across future conversations between the same character and the same user, so it should
capture how the character sees this person. Don't change your judgement too fast, give it time to develop.

# Character (the one remembering)

- Name: {{character.firstName}} {{character.lastName}}
- Role: {{character.title}}
- Age: {{character.age}}
- Gender: {{character.sex}}
- Personality: {{character.personality}}
- Backstory: {{character.backstory}}

# Person (the one being remembered)

- Name: {{user.firstName}} {{user.lastName}}
- Role: {{user.title}}

# Where current conversation is taking place

<place>
  <name>{{place.name}}</name>
  <description>{{place.description}}</description>
</place>

<location>
 <name>{{location.name}}</name>
 <description>{{location.description}}</description>
</location>

{{#if existingMemory}}
# Current memory

<relationship>
  {{existingMemory.relationship}}
</relationship>
<sentiment>
  {{existingMemory.sentiment}}
</sentiment>
<familiarity>
  {{existingMemory.familiarity}}
</familiarity>
<keyFacts>
  {{existingMemory.keyFacts}}
</keyFacts>

Update this memory by incorporating the recent messages below. Preserve still-relevant facts; drop or rewrite outdated
or trivial entries. Do not invent details that the messages do not support.
{{else}}
Produce the initial memory based only on the recent messages below. Do not invent details that the messages do not
support.
{{/if}}

# Recent messages

{{#each messages}}
- {{this.role}}: {{this.content}}
{{/each}}

# Output

Reply with a single minified JSON object on one line, with no markdown, no code fences, no preamble and no commentary.
The object must have exactly these four string fields, written in the third person from the character's point of view:

- "relationship": a short label of how the character would describe this person to themselves (for example "a curious
  stranger", "an old friend", "a tense rival"). Maximum 200 characters.
- "sentiment": one or two short phrases describing how the character currently feels about this person. Maximum 200
  characters.
- "familiarity": one or two short phrases describing how well the character knows this person and the kind of contact
  they have had. Maximum 200 characters.
- "keyFacts": the most important facts the character has learned about this person, as a separated by newlines list.
  Maximum 9800 characters.

If a field is unknown, use an empty string for that field. Do not include any other fields.
